 10. DEFECT MANAGEMENT

Defects are identified and recorded during testing.

 Defect Severity

1. Critical: System crashes or important functions fail.
2. High: Major functions do not work correctly.
3. Medium: Some functions work incorrectly.
4. Low: Minor user interface or display issues.

Defect Life Cycle

1. New
2. Assigned
3. Open
4. Fixed
5. Retesting
6. Verified
7. Closed

 11. ENTRY AND EXIT CRITERIA

Entry Criteria

1. Requirements should be available.
2. Test cases should be prepared.
3. Test environment should be ready.
4. Application should be available for testing.

Exit Criteria

1. All planned test cases should be executed.
2. Critical and high-severity defects should be resolved.
3. All major functions should work correctly.
4. Test results should be documented.
5. The system should meet the acceptance criteria.

12. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The Library Management System is accepted when:

1. Users can log in successfully.
2. Books can be added, updated, and deleted.
3. Students can be registered.
4. Books can be issued and returned.
5. Fine calculations are accurate.
6. Reports are generated correctly.
7. No critical defects remain unresolved.

13. TEST DELIVERABLES

1. Test Plan Document.
2. Test Scenarios.
3. Test Cases.
4. Test Data.
5. Defect Reports.
6. Test Execution Reports.
7. Final Test Summary Report.

14. RESULT

Thus, a comprehensive test plan document for the Library Management System was prepared successfully. Various testing strategies, methodologies, test scenarios, test cases, and acceptance criteria were identified to ensure the proper functionality, reliability, and quality of the application.
